       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. At that dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max IR dose)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg per administration\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical reason and I can add it as a note. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
